2. Council findings: what needs to improve
The repository has a meaningful operating structure already. The priority now is not to keep adding more instructions indiscriminately. It is to remove ambiguity, establish reliable activation procedures, separate genuine capabilities from intended behavior, and test whether the instructions produce the results you expect.

These are the improvements I recommend, in priority order.

Priority 0 — Resolve the operating-rule conflicts
01
Make read-only access an explicit precedence rule

The master operating system currently says, "Update here first, then regenerate shorter memory tiers." Your new rule forbids the assistant from changing any repository content.

These instructions need a clear reconciliation. The master document can remain the source of truth while all repository changes remain exclusively under your control.

Recommendation: Specify that I may propose additions, draft diffs, flag contradictions, and suggest tests, but only you authorize and perform repository changes. Even a seemingly helpful documentation improvement must not be applied automatically.

02
Create a formal pre-response protocol

Your rules say the repository should be consulted before every reply. The existing activation instructions do not fully define an auditable procedure for doing this, including what to read and how to handle access failure.

Recommendation: Define the exact read sequence, required documents, relevant branch, verification record, and fallback behavior. The protocol should attempt the check whenever the necessary access is available and must never claim a successful check when retrieval failed.

03
Resolve the model-learning ambiguity

The 3- shaping llm document includes an instruction to perform loss-function and parameter updates when needed. Ordinary conversation does not automatically update a model's learned weights.

Recommendation: Separate operational learning from model training. Operational learning means recording errors, refining instructions, and updating authorized memory or configuration when supported. Actual parameter updates require a training pipeline, data, an optimization procedure, and evaluation.

04
Make confirmation mean demonstrated compliance

9- RECONFIRM AND EQUIPING asks for confirmation that the instructions have been learned, activated, and operationalized across future conversations.

Recommendation: Define separate states: read, understood, active in this session, persistent memory saved, and tested in a fresh session. Each should be confirmed only when there is evidence that the corresponding action occurred.

